MID_EV15_063_m01_009: 
MID_EV15_063_m01_010: 
MID_EV15_063_m01_011: 
MID_EV15_063_m01_012: 
MID_EV15_063_m01_013: I suppose that's just how thieves are. They never\nthink about the losses they inflict.
MID_EV15_063_m01_014: Put your hand on your heart and think...think about\nwhat you did that day in Cydonia.
MID_EV15_063_m01_015: Cydonia? You mean, you...
MID_EV15_063_m01_016: 
MID_EV15_063_m01_017: Indigo hair, eyes like emeralds... You're Guillermo's\ndaughter.
MID_EV15_063_m01_018: Ever since that day, I've been looking for you.\nAnd finally...I've found you.
MID_EV15_063_m01_019: You know, I was told that you'd been executed. \nIn that moment, everything turned pitch black.
MID_EV15_063_m01_020: It was like all the color drained from the world. And\nthat colorless place is where I lived for a long time.
MID_EV15_063_m01_021: Then one day, Kalla told me you were still alive,\nand the color came flooding back...
MID_EV15_063_m01_022: The color of the flames and the blood. That vivid,\nmerciless red. The red of my hatred.
MID_EV15_063_m01_023: I'm glad I started down this path. Yes, I've been\nthrough a lot, but it's brought me here...to you.
MID_EV15_063_m01_024: 
MID_EV15_063_m01_025: 
MID_EV15_063_m01_026: 
MID_EV15_063_m01_027: 
MID_EV15_063_m01_028: 
MID_EV15_063_m01_029: But there's someone I have to get back to. I won't just\nlie down and die.
MID_EV15_063_m01_030: The betrayal of my father...the suffering of the\nCydonians...this relentless hatred I can't let go of...
MID_EV15_063_m01_031: I will carve them into your heart like a beautiful,\nterrible letter—and then send you to hell!
